Field names shadowed by method-local :DECLARE, :PARAMETERS and :PUBLIC
entries: the local is evidently intended, so neither
unqualified_field_assignment nor unqualified_field_read may fire. Qualified
Me: access elsewhere. Should be free of field findings.
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS Totaler;
:DECLARE nTotal, sLabel, aRows;

:PROCEDURE Compute;
	:DECLARE nTotal;
	nTotal := 5;
	:RETURN nTotal;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Rename;
	:PARAMETERS sLabel;
	Me:sLabel := sLabel;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Share;
	:PUBLIC aRows;
	aRows := {};
	:RETURN Len(Me:aRows);
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS Totaler;
:DECLARE nTotal, sLabel, aRows;

:PROCEDURE Compute;
	:DECLARE nTotal;
	nTotal := 5;
	:RETURN nTotal;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Rename;
	:PARAMETERS sLabel;
	Me:sLabel := sLabel;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Share;
	:PUBLIC aRows;
	aRows := {};
	:RETURN Len(Me:aRows);
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
16:2-16:9 info limit_public_vars: ':PUBLIC' variables persist across procedures and risk namespace pollution. Prefer ':DECLARE' with parameter passing
